      "content": "To spot these compliance-inducing frameworks, look for excessive abstraction paired with universalizing language. Watch for the heavy reliance on modal verbs implying destiny, such as \"must,\" \"will,\" or \"the only way to.\" Furthermore, any phrase that elevates the product beyond its function into a societal or personal *imperative*—like \"the new standard\" implying all others are obsolete—is a major marker. These structures are designed to make resistance feel like a failure of self.",
